<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  The ContentTools CMS, vendored.

  This is @jamesjnadeau/content-tools @@VERSION@@ (ContentTools @@SHA@@), copied out of
  that repository's `app/` and `dist/` by `scripts/sync-cms.sh`. It is
  committed rather than installed because the package is not on npm yet and
  its `dist/` is gitignored, so there is nothing to depend on. Refresh it
  with the script; do not hand-edit anything in this folder.

  The chunk filenames are CONTENT-HASHED, which is why the script deletes
  this folder before copying. Copy over the top instead and the old chunks
  stay behind while `shell.js` imports the new names -- a page that 404s on
  an import of a file nobody touched.

  `../cms-config.yml` is relative on purpose. This page is reachable at
  both `/admin/` and `/ContentTools-test/admin/` on Netlify, and only the
  second on Pages; a relative config resolves correctly at all three, and an
  absolute one would be wrong at two of them.

  The content stylesheet link is load-bearing, not decoration. In Mode A the
  editable content stays in the document, so its rules -- drop indicators,
  hover outlines, drag cursors -- have to reach the document too. Without it
  everything still LOOKS fine and none of the editing affordances appear.
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Content</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./content-tools-content.css">
<style>
    /* The page's only job is to give the shell the viewport. Everything
       else it draws is inside its own shadow root. */
    html, body { height: 100%; }
    body { margin: 0; }
    content-tools-cms { height: 100%; }
</style>
<script type="module" src="./shell.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<content-tools-cms config="../cms-config.yml"></content-tools-cms>
</body>
</html>
